WF-31 — Payment Submitted Handler

## Summary

- Inputs (WF-01 canonical envelope per data-contract-discipline Phase 1 — design.md §2.1): `phoneNumber` (E.164 string), `messageType`, `messageContent`, `user` (object: {id, phone_number, name, status, slack_channel_id, current_consultation_id}), `pendingUser` (null). Additional fields passed by WF-02: `messageText`, `userId`, `userStatus`. `user.name` used for Slack relay display; `user.slack_channel_id` used for Slack channel routing (no DB re-fetch required — envelope provides it).
- Outputs: On Branch A — for `general_enquiry` intent a Gemini-generated WhatsApp reply tailored to the payment-submitted stage; for other pass-through intents the canned "under review" reassurance via WF-50; for stop_intent a clarifier. On Branch B — Slack relay of the user message into the user's consult channel (unconditional). On Gemini General Response outage (Branch A) — sends user apology + dual admin alerts then halts via stopAndError (error propagates to WF-02 caller, but Branch B is parallel and may have already fired its Slack relay independently — acceptable).
- State Transitions: none. Auto-opt-out on Gemini-classified stop_intent removed 2026-05-23 (SP-04); explicit STOP keyword via WF-20 still unsubscribes canonically.
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-25 (Intent Classifier), WF-50 (Send WhatsApp), WF-51 (Send Slack — admin relay + halt-and-notify alerts)
- **Notes:**
  - **General-enquiry Gemini branch (2026-05-26 — GAP-3C):** `general_enquiry` intent on Branch A now routes to a Gemini-generated contextual reply with a payment-submitted stage cue and an email-callout (`chinmay_astro@gmail.com`). Other pass-through intents still get the canned "under review" reassurance. Branch B (Slack admin relay) is unaffected — fires unconditionally regardless of intent.
  - **Gemini General Response halt-and-notify (2026-05-27 — TD-PGF-09 scope expansion):** Identical pattern to WF-23/WF-30. HTTP node has `onError=continueErrorOutput`; on retries exhausted, error branch fans out to user apology (WF-50) + dual admin alerts (WF-51 consult + admin-commands), then `stopAndError` terminates Branch A. Payment-submitted users always have a consult Slack channel (Design Rule #2) — both alerts fire. Branch B may have already fired its Slack relay independently — acceptable.
  - **stop_intent policy (2026-05-23 — SP-04):** Gemini-classified stop_intent no longer auto-routes to WF-47 unsubscribe. Clarifier message sent instead. Literal STOP still flows through WF-20.
  - **Provably dead-code branch removed 2026-05-23 (SP-04):** the previous `Is Stop Intent?` IF's FALSE branch was unreachable per the WF-25 contract.
  - Two parallel branches: Branch A intent path + Branch B unconditional Slack admin relay. Slack relay fires for every inbound message in `payment_submitted` state.
  - **Load User for Relay removed (Phase 1):** `slack_channel_id` is now read from envelope. The `Load User for Relay` Postgres node has been removed.
  - **Call WF-25 envelope add-on (2026-05-27 — TD-PGF-05):** previously `workflowInputs.value` was empty (passthrough-via-trigger pattern). Now explicit 6-field mapping per data-contract-discipline: phoneNumber, userId, messageText, userStatus, userName (`user.name`), slackChannelId (`user.slack_channel_id`). WF-25 reads these for its halt-and-notify alert template.
  - WF-25 caller field name (TD-DRIFT-009): caller passes `messageText`; WF-25 reads `messageContent` — explicitly deferred from Phase 1 per §1.5.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — Triggered by parent with WF-01 canonical envelope plus {messageText, userId, userStatus}. Read `phoneNumber` and `user.slack_channel_id` from envelope directly (no DB re-fetch).
Step 2: Fan out in parallel from trigger:
  - Branch A → GOTO Step 3 (intent classification + user reply)
  - Branch B → GOTO Step 21 (admin Slack relay)

(Branch A — user reply)
Step 3: Call WF-25 with 6 fields: phoneNumber, userId, messageText, userStatus, userName (from `user.name`), slackChannelId (from `user.slack_channel_id`). Receive intentResult.
Step 4: Check `Is Pass-Through Intent?` — is intentResult NOT one of {garbage, malicious_abusive, inappropriate, stop_intent}?
  - If YES → GOTO Step 5
  - If NO (only stop_intent reachable per WF-25 contract) → GOTO Step 19
Step 5: Check `Is General Enquiry?` — is intentResult == "general_enquiry"?
  - If YES → GOTO Step 6
  - If NO → GOTO Step 18
Step 6: Build Gemini prompt instructing a helpful, warm assistant for Chinmay's Vedic astrology consultation service on WhatsApp, with the user-stage cue "user has submitted payment which is now being reviewed by Dr. Chinmay" and the email-callout cue "they can email chinmay_astro@gmail.com if something urgent comes up". Ask Gemini to weave both naturally into a brief 2-3 sentence reply. Append the user's messageContent.
Step 7: POST to Gemini (gemini-2.5-flash-lite) with temperature=0.3, maxOutputTokens=200, timeout=10s, retryOnFail=true, maxTries=3, onError=continueErrorOutput. On success: GOTO Step 8. On retries exhausted (error output): GOTO Step 9 (halt-and-notify).
Step 8: Extract Gemini reply text from candidates[0].content.parts[0].text; fallback "Thank you for your message! For questions about our Vedic astrology consultation, feel free to ask." Call WF-50 with { phoneNumber, messageType="text", messageContent=reply } per §2.3 canonical contract. End of Branch A.
Step 9: Build user apology WF-50 payload per §2.3 — { phoneNumber, messageType="text", messageContent="Sorry — we ran into a brief technical issue and couldn't process your message just now. Dr. Chinmay has been notified and will follow up with you shortly. We apologise for the inconvenience." }.
Step 10: Call WF-50 (apology to user). Continue to admin alert chain.
Step 11: Build admin alert text (Code) — translate userStatus to plain English (payment_submitted → "payment under review"). Resolve userName. Construct General Response failure variant messageText. Emit { messageText }.
Step 12: Check `Has Consult Channel?` — is `user.slack_channel_id` non-empty (notEmpty unary)?
  - If YES → GOTO Step 13.
  - If NO → GOTO Step 15.
Step 13: Build consult alert payload — { channelId: `user.slack_channel_id`, messageText: `$('Build Admin Alert Text').item.json.messageText` }.
Step 14: Call WF-51 (consult-channel alert). GOTO Step 15.
Step 15: Build admin-commands alert payload — { channelId: "C0A5B0ZE81E", messageText: `$('Build Admin Alert Text').item.json.messageText` }.
Step 16: Call WF-51 (admin-commands alert). GOTO Step 17.
Step 17: stopAndError — terminate Branch A.
Step 18: (pass-through non-general-enquiry path — from Step 5 NO branch) Build "under review" message: "⏳ Your payment is currently under review. Chinmay will verify it and get back to you shortly (usually within a few hours). You don't need to do anything else right now. If you have any questions, feel free to ask!" Call WF-50 with { phoneNumber, messageType="text", messageContent=the message } per §2.3 canonical contract. End of Branch A.
Step 19: (stop_intent path — from Step 4 NO branch) Build WF-50 stop-intent clarifier payload per §2.3 canonical contract:
  - phoneNumber = <phoneNumber> (from top-level envelope)
  - messageType = "text"
  - messageContent = "This is an automated message from Chinmay Astro — we noticed your message mentioned STOP or unsubscribing. If this was unrelated, please ignore. If you do want to opt out of this service, simply send STOP at any time."
Step 20: Call WF-50 (Stop Clarifier) with the prepared payload. End of Branch A.

(Branch B — relay user message into Slack consult channel, with aging tag)
Step 21: SELECT created_at FROM chinmay_astro.payments WHERE user_id = user.id ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1. If no row found, treat elapsed as `?`.
Step 22: Compute elapsed-since-paid as a human string: `< 60 min` → `{n} min ago`; `< 24 h` → `{n} h ago`; else `{n} d ago`.
Step 23: Read `user.slack_channel_id` from the WF-01 envelope. Build relay payload: { channelId=user.slack_channel_id, messageText="⏱ Paid {elapsed} · 💬 *Message from <user.name or phoneNumber> (payment under review):*\n><messageContent>" }.
Step 24: Call WF-51 (Send Slack) with { channelId, messageText } per §2.4 canonical contract. End of Branch B.
